From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NP <50584693+NatePu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:57:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] T1.1: net.flow sysctl plumbing

- sys/socket.h: pseudo_AF_FLOW 37, AF_MAX 38, PF_FLOW; CTL_NET_NAMES gets
  a { 0, 0 } placeholder for AF_FRAME (36) and "flow" (37).
- net/if_flow.h: FLOWCTL_* and FLOWCTL_NAMES, outside _KERNEL.
- kern/uipc_domain.c: PF_FLOW branch in net_sysctl(), inside
  #ifndef SMALL_KERNEL and #if NFLOW > 0.
- net/if_flow.c: flow_sysctl() with sysctl_int_bounded() and the SPEC 6.1
  bounds (ERRATA E82); mode through a flow_ctl_lock-serialised setter
  running the DESIGN 5.7 transition skeleton; mode 2 EOPNOTSUPP before
  anything changes; max only in mode 0 (EBUSY); budget/yield stored
  while off and applied through the transition when active; yield stored
  after the MD rounding op (ERRATA E81); flow_gen_bump().
- net/if_flowvar.h: fmo_yield_round in the MD ops.
- sbin/sysctl: net.flow names, PF_FLOW case and sysctl_flow().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
